# Quiz System: Instructor App (Electron)

- LAN-only. Must work with NO internet. No CDNs, cloud services, or online APIs. Bundle all assets.
- Stack: TypeScript, Electron (electron-vite, React template), Fastify + WebSocket for the embedded server, SQLite later (not yet). Don't swap the stack.
- docs/protocol.md is the source of truth for messages. Never invent or change message types without updating it first.
- The server is authoritative: it owns timers, pause state, and scoring. Answer keys never go to phones.
- Instructor commands come only from the local UI via IPC. Never accept instructor commands over the WebSocket.
- Build only the current step. No extra features, no speculative abstractions.
- Keep the server code in src/main/server and UI code in src/renderer.
- Write small, readable modules. Add brief comments only where the logic is not obvious.